  description: A mobile phone identified in the case file as belonging to the victim.
  foundLocation: On the floor within the documented scene area.
  observedCondition: The phone was found screen-down. Its exterior was preserved
    for handling-trace examination and its stored records were not assumed from its
    position.
  investigativeContext: Device records may provide a timeline or communication context
    when lawfully examined and corroborated. The phone's position alone cannot establish
    how it came to rest there.
  loggingContext: 'Recovered Messages


    "We can''t keep meeting like this. She
    is already suspicious."

    "I know. I''ll explain everything after tonight."

    "Delete
    these messages. I don''t want anyone finding out."


    The recovered conversation
    suggests that the victim was involved in a personal relationship outside the
    marriage.


    This is a fictional case record created for training purposes.'
